    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 10,
    "excerpt": "We are Asian Paints, delivering joy since 1942. We are in the business of colour, décor, design and protection, we make anything & everything beautiful and lasting. Being innovators, we transcend global boundaries and are the preferred brand. We are dynamic and disruptive. Constantly redefining trends with world-class solutions, inspiring consumers",
    "section": "Corporate overview"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 73,
    "excerpt": "Asian Paints strengthened its design capabilities through Chromacosm, the world’s largest architectural colour system, offering over 5,300 shades in a structured palette. Designed for architects, designers and homeowners, it enables seamless visualisation across tonal variations, supporting more precise and consistent design outcomes.",
    "section": "Corporate overview"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "ar-2026",
    "page": 4,
    "excerpt": "From leveraging advanced colour systems like Chromacosm - the world's largest colour system, to pioneering premium décor offerings through Nilaya Anthology, we are shaping the future of interior aesthetics. Our innovations encompass platforms like the Glitz Guide, to new introductions across paint, waterproofing, lights and kitchen categories, spreading joy in every corner.",
    "section": "Management discussion and analysis"
   }
  ],
  "segments": null,
  "management": [
   {
    "sourceId": "call-2026-08",
    "page": 24,
    "excerpt": "The strategy going forward is that we really get growth in every segment which is there, because while the overall premium segment is important to us, the economy segment is also large. That is also very important that we are able to grow it. Putty is a starting point of paints.",
    "speaker": "Amit Syngle"
   },
   {
    "sourceId": "call-2026-08",
    "page": 11,
    "excerpt": "When we look at premiumization, we have been able to galvanize a lot of products from the point of view of upgrading the customer to a higher level and premiumization has been a route, not only in the premium segment but also in the luxury segment.",
    "speaker": "Amit Syngle"
   }
  ]
